    "narrative": "The clear engine of the offense for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads all starters with an elite 77.63 score against McGreevy. The combination of a favorable SP_xERA of 4.43 and a premium #2 spot in the order maximizes his stolen base potential, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. **Vinnie Pasquantino** follows closely with a 66.63 score; despite the wait for a confirmed lineup, the projected platoon advantage against Troy Melton (3.85 xERA) makes him a cornerstone play. **Gabriel Moreno** also provides stability behind the dish (60.15), buoyed by a favorable matchup and high recency form, making this trio the bedrock of today\u2019s projected production.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with **Zach McKinstry** (55.54) and **Austin Riley** (53.73). **Zach McKinstry** benefits significantly from the soft 5.65 xERA of Randy Dobnak, though his lower spot in the lineup caps his upside. **Austin Riley** enters as a marginal start; while his raw talent is high, the matchup against Hart is neutral, and we are forced to monitor his output closely. Among our depth, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak** are all unavailable today due to team off-days. Given the current bench composition, our secondary prospects like **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain in reserve to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable platoon splits later in the week.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Zach McKinstry**. If those lineup positions shift downward, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating a shift toward bench depth\u2014though options like **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, or **Henry Bolte** are currently being held to prioritize **Trevor Story**-level utility in tighter matchups. The primary risk today is volatility from the bottom of the order, so we will be monitoring the real-time scoring data to determine if any underperforming starters require an early hook to save roster efficiency for the weekend push.",
